# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allowlist, not a blocklist.
#
# This folder holds roughly 4.9 GB that must never enter git: Model/ (1.8 GB of
# .3dm, several files over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit), Data/ (1.8 GB of
# shapefiles and energy exports), Presentations/ (556 MB) and ~730 MB of loose
# media in the root. Ignoring everything and re-including only the code makes an
# accidental `git add .` impossible rather than merely unlikely.
#
# The large inputs stay on disk. What the code derives from them is small and IS
# committed - Dashboard/public/buildings.geojson, Dashboard/src/data/*.json - so
# a clone can render the campus without them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
# How to run the table on a machine that is not this one. It spans the backend
# and MR-Table both, so it sits at the root rather than inside either.
!/RUNNING-THE-TABLE.md

!/Dashboard/
!/ECOM Toolkit/
!/Optimization/
/Optimization/*
!/Optimization/LEC-Opt/
!/Optimization/GH_Components/

# The ACE MR Studio interactive map (Nodal-Works/interactive_map, branch dev),
# grafted with its history. Its media/ is ~169 MB of demo video, GIFs and STL
# meshes; that is large but every file is under GitHub's 100 MB limit and the
# app will not run without it, so it is committed rather than ignored.
!/MR-Table/

# LEC-Opt ships sample workbooks; they are small and belong with the model.
# Its own .gitignore still applies inside that tree.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standard build and environment noise, wherever it appears
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/dist/
**/dist-ssr/
**/.vite/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.local
**/*.log

# Fetched at runtime and reproducible; some of it is large. The Gurobi licence
# written from .env lands in cache/gurobi/ and is covered by this too.
Dashboard/backend/cache/

# Machine settings and secrets: which solver this machine uses, and the Gurobi
# licence that makes it legal. The example beside it IS committed, and carries
# no licence - see Dashboard/backend/.env.example.
**/.env
**/.env.local
!**/.env.example
**/gurobi.lic

# Editor and OS
# Personal editor state stays out; how to run this project does not. The Live
# Server root, its /api proxy and the backend task are facts about the table,
# not preferences - without them Go Live serves the pages on an origin with no
# backend behind it, which looks like a broken dashboard rather than a missing
# setting.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
